{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id289169571"}, "name":{"label":"Wolverinezzz"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-05-16T03:07:25-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.88.1"}, "id":{"label":"12661800370"}, "title":{"label":"Recommended -easy and fun. Fair amount of free access"}, "content":{"label":"Nice simple little app that can actually be used for free if you don’t want to have full customisation. Essentially, if you are happy to forgo the full app customisation and the extra data that being able to distinguish negative  effects of caffeine and alcohol (and the positive effects of milk) on overall hydration you can use this app very comfortably for free.\n\nI don’t understand when people complain about apps, or features within them, costing money though. The developer’s need paying (who doesn’t?) and there is no obligation to buy if you don’t think it’s a fair deal.  It’s a free market and since there are no annoying ads ruining this app it’s quite reasonable to be invited to pay for the advanced features. If I like it enough I may just pay for the full version later but for now I can get an idea about whether it’s worth it to me which seems a fair deal. \n\nAlso, the developers have done a nice Apple Watch version which has the bare bones features which makes it very useable on the watch.\nYou can also allow the app to update Apple’s Health app with your water intake if you choose.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=1454778585&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
